   "The storm came in from the sea at dusk, dragging a curtain of black cloud across the harbour. The first drops were fat and heavy, smacking into the dust like thrown coins. Then the sky split open. Rain hammered the rooftops, drummed on car bonnets and turned the gutters into brown, gurgling rivers that swallowed litter and leaves in a single gulp.",
   "The city, which had been sweltering and sluggish all afternoon, jolted awake. Shopkeepers scrambled to drag their displays inside. Pedestrians scattered like startled pigeons, newspapers held uselessly over their heads. Only the children were delighted: they leapt from puddle to puddle, shrieking, faces tilted to the sky as if the rain were a gift that had been promised to them for months.",
