   "Mrs Farah’s shop was barely wider than a corridor, but it seemed to contain the whole world. Shelves climbed to the ceiling, crammed with jars of pickles, tins of sardines, spools of thread, torch batteries and faded packets of seeds. The air was thick with the smells of cardamom, soap and old paper. A single bulb swung above the counter, and in its warm, trembling light everything seemed slightly magical, as if the shop had been assembled by a collector of lost things.",
